; the limit of 3x + 1 for x going to 2 is 7, by the limit laws of analysis.kurt instead of ε and
; δ (as in limit-of-linear-function.kurt): `tends x a L T` says that the limit exists and is `L`
load analysis

tends x 2 2 x                                       ; tends-id
tends x 2 (3 * 2) (3 * x)                           ; tends-scale
tends x 2 1 1                                       ; tends-const
tends x 2 (3 * 2 + 1) (3 * x + 1)                   ; tends-add
calc on
tends x 2 7 (3 * x + 1)
calc off
lim x 2 (3 * x + 1) = 7                             ; tends-lim
; `lim` alone says nothing: it has a value for every argument (no limit of 1/x at 0 exists)
expect "ProofError"
    tends x 0 (lim x 0 (1 / x)) (1 / x)
